@startuml
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Segoe UI
skinparam defaultFontSize 11
skinparam ArrowColor #0b7a75
skinparam ComponentBorderColor #0b7a75
skinparam DatabaseBorderColor #6b7280
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #f3f4f6
skinparam NoteBorderColor #9ca3af

skinparam sequence {
  ParticipantBorderColor #0b7a75
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #eef6f5
  ParticipantFontColor #0b3b39
  LifeLineBorderColor #9ca3af
  ActorBorderColor #0b7a75
  ActorBackgroundColor #eef6f5
  BoxBorderColor #9ca3af
  BoxBackgroundColor #fdfdfd
}
skinparam maxMessageSize 200
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true

title FindCare → EvaluateCare Handoff Sequence\nTarget front-application architecture\n2026-09-15

actor "Consumer\n(Browser)" as user
box "SharedServices (main)" #fdfdfd
participant "Gate\n(facade)" as gate
participant "Universal\nNavigator" as nav
participant "Utterance\nManager" as um
participant "Prose\nTool (?)" as prose
end box
box "FindCare (satellite)" #eef6f5
participant "UN Proxy\n+ provider tools" as fc
end box
box "EvaluateCare (satellite)" #eef6f5
participant "UN Proxy\n+ scoring tools" as ec
end box
database "MongoDB\nregistry · sessions\nledger · data" as db

note over gate, db
  The Gate is the only transport-aware node. The UniversalNavigator holds no data:
  the map is the live registry document, parameters ride the passed document,
  sessions and the render ledger are repository rows. Every throw ends in a navigator.
end note

note over um, prose #ffe9cc
  OPEN ARCHITECTURAL QUESTION — NOT RESOLVED.
  Is user-facing prose (asking the user a question and authoring the sentence)
  the UtteranceManager's own scope, or a separate "Prose" tool?
  Three approved requirements place prose inside the UtteranceManager
  (EPIC-002-F-010-S-001, -S-003, EPIC-006-F-008-S-003); the registry instance
  carries a "Prose" route name. This diagram draws Prose as a separate tool to
  show ONE candidate shape only — the split is the operator's to decide.
end note

== Startup (once per build) ==
nav -> db : read this env's live registry doc
db -> nav : the one map\n(tools · routes · may_call)
nav -> fc : hand proxy its metadata slice
nav -> ec : hand proxy its metadata slice

== Phase 1: Sessioned request arrives ==
user -> gate : client_sessioned call\nsession token + params
gate -> nav : token, HTTP head, params\n(nothing else)
nav -> db : maintain / verify session
nav -> nav : parameters vs state\n(a conflict is an exception)

== Phase 2: Route the utterance ==
nav -> um : dispatch utterance
note right of um
  Preamble (cached system prompt)
  + every tool's registry fragment.
  One model call, routes out.
  Knows no parameters.
end note
um -> nav : dispatch set\n(target_actions)
nav -> nav : validate selection vs\nmay_call + dependency map

== Phase 3: Provider search — FindCare satellite ==
nav -> nav : completeness test\n(required inputs present?)
nav -> nav : record expectation\nin render ledger
nav -> fc : dispatch provider_search\ntool_to_tool, crosses the wire
fc -> db : vector search\nprovider data
db -> fc : provider results
fc -> nav : internal_callback (our_signature)\ncloses its ledger entry
nav -> nav : serial deterministic merge

== Phase 4: Handoff to evaluation — EvaluateCare satellite ==
nav -> nav : completeness test\nfor evaluate_providers
nav -> ec : dispatch evaluate_providers\ntool_to_tool, crosses the wire
ec -> db : read quality signals per NPI\n(certs, CMS scores, actions)
db -> ec : quality signals
ec -> ec : score + rank providers
ec -> nav : internal_callback (our_signature)\ncloses its ledger entry
nav -> nav : serial deterministic merge

== Phase 5: User-facing prose (see open question above) ==
nav -> prose : author prose from merged facts\n(as a Prose tool, OR folded into the UtteranceManager)
prose -> nav : internal_callback\nthe user-facing sentence
nav -> nav : merge

== Phase 6: One stream back ==
nav -> nav : render ledger complete\n(timeout facts race the callbacks)
nav -> gate : sequenced answer\n(the one stream)
gate -> user : stream ranked evaluation\n+ prose

note over user, db
  No business logic on the client and no direct FindCare→EvaluateCare call:
  cross-server traffic is tool_to_tool through each satellite's proxy, answers
  return as internal callbacks, and the main sequences, merges, and streams once.
end note

@enduml
